{#- uid/gid pinned to the `ntfy` system account (pillar/ntfy.sls): the image
   runs as root by default; the container runs as this account instead
   (Podman `User=`, mapped 1:1), so the data dir stays owned by it on the
   host. The matching formulas/users account entry must use the same numbers.

   Auth is declarative (ntfy `auth-users`/`auth-access`/`auth-tokens` in
   server.yml): ntfy syncs users, ACLs and tokens from the config into its
   auth DB on every start and deletes what isn't listed. Secret values are
   empty here on purpose — pillar fills them from OpenBao; empty or
   unresolved fails config.sls (ntfy never starts without them).
     admin_password_hash / publisher_password_hash: bcrypt ($2a$/$2b$/$2y$,
       cost >= 10), not the password itself.
     publisher_token is tk_ + 29 chars of [-_A-Za-z0-9].
   publisher_topics: topic patterns (`*` wildcard) the publisher may write.
   extra_publishers: further write-only users, one per sending service
   (never share the Alertmanager token): list of {user, password_hash,
   token, topics}, same formats as above. Each listed entry is validated
   like the three secrets — pillar only lists one once its secrets exist.
   default_access: what everyone else (anonymous) gets — deny-all.
   http_port: host port; ntfy listens on 8080 inside (non-root, no
   CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for :80).
   podman: spec overrides for the container (keys: formulas/podman README). #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'image': 'docker.io/binwiederhier/ntfy',
    'tag': 'v2.37.2',
    'container_name': 'ntfy',
    'uid': 974,
    'gid': 974,
    'http_port': 8090,
    'base_dir': '/opt/ntfy',
    'config_dir': '/opt/ntfy/config',
    'data_dir': '/opt/ntfy/data',
    'base_url': '',
    'cache_duration': '12h',
    'default_access': 'deny-all',
    'admin_user': 'admin',
    'admin_password_hash': '',
    'publisher_user': 'alertmanager',
    'publisher_password_hash': '',
    'publisher_token': '',
    'publisher_topics': ['alerts-*'],
    'extra_publishers': [],
    'podman': {},
} %}
{%- set ntfy = salt['pillar.get']('ntfy:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
